---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { profile } from "../data/profile";
import { labFigures } from "../data/lab-figures";
import { projectClips } from "../data/lab-projects";
const surgeryFigures = ["surgical-workspace", "restricted-viewpoints", "obscured-view", "surgery-mechanism", "eye-concept", "eyelid-concept", "soft-nozzle", "cleaning-control", "ai-pipeline", "spatial-feedback"];
const surgeryClips = projectClips.filter(clip => clip.project === "surgery-ai");
---

<Layout title="Accessibility | Songyang Liu">
  <div class="page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Using this website</p><h1>Accessibility</h1><p>
      This personal website is designed with WCAG 2.1 Level A and AA
      requirements in mind. Accessibility is an ongoing effort; automated checks
      do not constitute a complete compliance certification.
    </p>
  </div>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="navigation">
    <h2 id="navigation">Navigation & reading</h2><p>
      A skip link leads to the main content. Links and figure descriptions can
      be operated with a keyboard, and focused controls have a visible outline.
      The layout adapts to narrow screens and increased text spacing. Research
      images include alternative text and expandable descriptions.
    </p><p>
      The academic CV is provided as an HTML web edition. The homepage and CV
      contain still images. The locally hosted project pages present images, diagrams, and videos with native controls.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="section" id="project-media" aria-labelledby="project-media-heading">
    <h2 id="project-media-heading">Project videos & source materials</h2>
    <p>The Architected Structures, AI-Empowered Healthy Built Environments, Building Immunology, Robotic Disinfection, Surgery AI, Robotic Block Assembly, and Disease-Resistant School Communities pages use supplied research presentations, videos, and earlier DreamXLab project materials. Informative images have alternative text and longer explanations. Each video has an accessible text alternative and a timed WebVTT description track. Readable video descriptions and source credits are collected in the project’s Sources & media notes section. Figures can be opened at their original resolution. Research diagrams retain their original colors; labels and text explain their meaning independently of color.</p>
    <p>Videos can start muted when visible and pause outside the viewport or in a hidden tab. Native controls support manual playback and pause; manual pause is remembered. Reduced-motion and data-saving preferences disable automatic playback. Keyboard users can Tab to a video and use Space to play or pause it. Native controls also remain available without JavaScript.</p>
    <p>The web excerpts retain complete frames and original motion speed. The digital-twin model animations have no audio. The surgical concept animations have digitally silent audio tracks. Laboratory sounds are omitted from the benchtop excerpt, which is presented as a silent visual demonstration. The Robotic Disinfection infographic excerpts also omit source audio and provide text alternatives for the illustrated workflow; publisher and paper credits remain visible. Original media remain unchanged in the supplied files and source repository.</p>
    <p>The School Communities film retains its original English narration and music, starts muted, and provides default English captions, a full transcript and timed visual descriptions. It plays once rather than looping. Captions were compared across two local transcription passes, word timestamps and source material; independent listening and screen-reader review remain outstanding. The film presents historical school-modeling scenarios and retains its original research credits.</p>
    <p>These pages distinguish project goals, hardware illustrations, and demonstration footage from evidence in cited publications. Building Immunology and Robotic Disinfection retain the original bibliography authors; these are not presented as Songyang Liu’s personal publication list. The case selectors use keyboard-operable buttons and keep all cases visible when JavaScript is unavailable. Recorded interface screenshots are labeled as archived examples. Full screen-reader usability and external PDF reading order have not been certified.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="section" id="surgery-media" aria-labelledby="surgery-media-heading">
    <h2 id="surgery-media-heading">Surgery AI images & videos</h2>
    <p>The magnetic camera footage documents a laboratory prototype. The Eye Concept, robotic eyelid, soft nozzle and cleaning controller are proposed designs. The AI examples come from a separate simulation training study; integration with camera actuation and lens care remains a research goal. On the project page, these descriptions are available to screen readers beside each image and video.</p>
    <p>Figures 2 and 7 are reproduced from <a href="https://arxiv.org/html/2511.02233v1">Liu, Tan and Li’s spatial-awareness training paper</a> under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">Creative Commons Attribution 4.0</a>, converted to WebP without cropping.</p>
    {surgeryFigures.map(id => { const figure = labFigures[id]; return <><h3>{figure.title}</h3><p>{figure.description}</p><p>Source: {figure.source}</p></>; })}
    {surgeryClips.map(clip => <><h3>{clip.title}</h3><p>{clip.description} {clip.audioNote}</p><p>Source: <a href={`https://github.com/DreamXLab/DreamXLab.github.io/blob/c4a06d081f7f22f9966cbc5248b7ceb61de8c842/${clip.sourceFile}`}>DreamXLab’s original recording</a>; {clip.sourceRange}. Original speed and complete frame retained.</p></>)}
  </section>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="attachments">
    <h2 id="attachments">Research papers & external websites</h2><p>
      Paper links open publisher or repository pages that may offer HTML and PDF
      versions. Project pages are linked separately. Their content and
      accessibility can differ from this website. PDF tagging, reading order,
      equations, and screen-reader compatibility have not been fully verified
      for external publications.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="checks">
    <h2 id="checks">Testing</h2><p>
      Release checks include axe scans targeting WCAG 2.1 A and AA, keyboard
      navigation, 320 CSS-pixel reflow, increased text spacing, image
      descriptions, and heading structure. Manual review remains necessary,
      including evaluation with assistive technology.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="help">
    <h2 id="help">Report an accessibility issue</h2><p>
      If a page, figure, or linked publication is difficult to access, email <a
        href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a
      > with the page address and the information you need. Please include your browser
      or assistive technology if relevant.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
